                StoryPart(2, "The Work Order", listOf(
                    "The parks officer explained that the bench had become unsafe and was being assessed for replacement. The old timber could not simply be put back. Tobi asked whether the council planned to install another bench in the same place. The officer said the team was reviewing the layout because visitors had asked for a more accessible seating area.",
                    "The students requested permission to research the bench's history for a class project. The parks office provided a public work-order summary and an old photograph of the tree. The photograph showed that the bench had been donated by a residents' association many years earlier. A small plaque had recorded the donation."
